raygui
------
  Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raygui
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license, the same license as this project.

  This project DOES vendor and redistribute raygui.
  raygui-sys/vendor/raygui.h is an unmodified copy of upstream's single-file
  header at revision 5.0-9-gfbf5d95, and raygui-sys/vendor/styles/*.rgs are
  unmodified copies of six of upstream's style themes. Each .rgs carries an
  embedded font, which is likewise upstream's.

  raygui is header-only, so there is no shared library to install and no
  package-manager formula for it anywhere. raygui-sys/vendor/raygui_impl.c is
  the one compilation unit that instantiates the implementation, and it is the
  whole of the C in this project. raygui-sys/jank-build.bb compiles it during
  the build. Vendoring the header is what pins the version and makes that
  build reproducible.

  Four examples in raygui-examples/src/net/b12n/raygui_jnk/ are jank ports of
  raygui's own example programs: scroll-panel, floating-window,
  custom-input-box and style-selector. Those are likewise zlib/libpng
  licensed, and this project is released under the same license so that the
  original terms carry through.

raylib
------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
  https://github.com/raysan5/raylib
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

  This project does not vendor or redistribute raylib. It arrives as the
  package org.jank-lang.commons/raylib-sys, which builds raylib from source at
  dependency-resolution time, and raygui-sys links against that build.

  raygui-sys/src/net/b12n/raygui_jnk/raylib.jank is a small helper namespace
  covering window lifecycle, screenshots and style-path resolution. It is
  written for this project rather than derived from another repo's bindings,
  because jank reaches raylib through raylib.h directly and needs no bindings
  layer to derive from.

